  "$comment": "EXP-1270 (EXP-1259 D6): Getting started x4 = ONE block: a header row (the title `title`, the muted `{done} of {total}`, a `meter` px wide progress meter, trailing a Docs button (`docs.label`, concept `docs.icon`, opens `docs.url`)) over ONE row of square cards in `steps` order (pointer: wrapping never, the row scrolls horizontally when narrower than its cards; phones: a horizontal scroll strip of the same cards). A card is `card.width`x`card.height` at radius lg with the card hairline: the step icon top-left, top-right a green check when done or the muted step NUMBER (its 1-based position in the visible list) when not, the title bottom-left (13px medium, two lines max); the NEXT step (first not done) is highlighted (filled with the hover fill + a foreground hairline at 30%), done cards keep the check and stay clickable (do it again); no descriptions, no locked state, no per-card buttons. A click runs the step's `target` (a step with `needsDevice` and no device opens `add-device` instead); targets: create-board = the create-board dialog, github = the GitHub connect step (web /integrations/github, desktop Settings > Repositories, phones open the web page), add-device = the ONE device-setup block, agent = the Agent page with the composer focused, invite = the invite dialog, add-server = the device-setup block on its server tab, mcp = the per-client MCP setup instructions in a dialog (web + IDE; done once an MCP grant or API key exists), widget = Settings > Widget. Visibility: `visibleWhen` names a permission (owner-only surfaces); `phones: false` steps never render on iOS/Android. Where it shows: on an EMPTY board (under the empty state), on the Agent home while the team has NO board (composer-home.json), and behind the sidebar entry `Getting started` (web + IDE rail; phones: the More tab row), which opens the same block in a centred dialog (phones: a bottom sheet); the web right sheet is gone. The block (and the entry) disappears once `complete`. Removed x4 with it: the lightbulb suggestion surfaces (action-suggestion concept rows), the action suggestion seeds (action-suggestions.ts + the natives) and the composer's suggestion rows. Model = pure `deriveGettingStarted(signals, permissions, platform)` (web components/getting-started/getting-started-model.ts, desktop getting_started.rs, iOS GettingStartedProgress.swift, Android GettingStartedModel.kt), every mirror replays `cases` (compare the WHOLE expected object).",
